WEBVTT

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.020
<i>The Enlightened One: Buddha.</i>

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.930
<i>The Son of God: Jesus.</i>

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.840
<i>In order to lead people to salvation,</i>

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.290
<i>the two of them were strict at times, gentle at others,</i>

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.950
<i>and spread teachings that would place people on the path to prosperity.</i>

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:38.510
<i>Those teachings, which became the foundations of Buddhism and Christianity,</i>

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.610
<i>continue to guide the lives of many even today.</i>

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>However...</i>

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.470
Hey!

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.910
<i>A person capable of uttering words that could instill fear in even them existed.</i>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.280
You can't take the trash out until <i>after</i> you sort it!

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.250
Can't you see it clearly written right here?!

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.430
I-I'm so sorry!

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:11.050
<i>Yes, here at Tachikawa City's Matsuda Heights,</i>

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:11.050
Matsuda
Heights

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.500
<i>the 64-year-old landlady, Matsuda Sachiyo, quietly rules over it.</i>

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:18.400
Scary.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.890
Saint☆Young Men.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.060
Commandments

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.370
<i>Commandments.</i>

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:35.240
Matsuda Heights' Commandments
You must pay your rent
You must take your trash out on time
after sorting it
You mustn't forget your daily greetings
You mustn't disturb others with loudness
You must respect your parents
You mustn't disturb your neighbors
You mustn't incite an assembly
You mustn't keep a pet
You mustn't feed stray animals
Those who do not follow these rules
will be evicted

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>They are oaths to govern oneself with,</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.550
<i>as well as rules that facilitate harmonious communal living.</i>

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.710
G-Good morning.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.100
Yes, good morning to you too.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.130
Oh?

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.510
Looks like you two are being responsible.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.430
It's the natural thing to do as tenants.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.060
Doesn't your company have any sort of dress code?!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.310
Company?

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.220
Oh, I believe that's one way to refer to a workplace.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.150
Well, Buddha?

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.610
When practicing asceticism in forests, outfits even more casual than this would actually be fine though.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.400
Don't tell me... You two...

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.450
You're not performers in a band or something, right?

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.620
Of course not.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.050
Honestly, music doesn't suit us.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.590
If anything, I would say Heart Sutra—

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.850
Oh, at any rate, we'll be fine, so please don't be concerned.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:44.140
Matsuda
Heights

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.570
Well then, we'll be off to take out the trash now.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.470
Heart Sutra?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.850
Something seems fishy here.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.010
They don't seem like bad people, but...

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.220
Those two have strange rumors about them floating around.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.280
Ninja! Ninja!

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.960
He was steadily walking on the surface of a river.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.320
"Walking on the surface of a river"?

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.410
Couldn't you two have just been drunk?

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.800
No! No!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.300
Oh, that street performer.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.800
I saw him together with a snake on a rainy day like this.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.360
"Together with a snake"?

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.040
Don't you think it's time to get new glasses?

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.690
No! No!

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.340
"He was seriously floating,"

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.410
is what the girls in our class were saying about him.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.060
Those two <i>do</i> always seem to be floating above the crowd.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:45.870
Indeed.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.620
"He was shining too,"

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.600
is what Abe from Class 4 was saying about him.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.720
So he <i>was</i> wearing a wig.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.750
What a shame when he's still young.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.280
And he's ping-pong, you know.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.930
He's definitely ping-pong.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.210
Super ping-pong.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.780
He's ping-pong and an alien from planet Button, right?

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:05.730
UFO.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.690
"Ping-pong and an alien from planet Button"?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.440
I-It's my fault, so...

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.450
That's beyond fishy.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.670
Not to mention, when they first moved in...

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Contract

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Tenant

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Address

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Afterlife, Heaven City 1st District House Number 1

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Regarding the aforementioned, the first party,
the landlord, and the second
party, the tenants...
concluded as thus.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Co-signer

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.220
Maybe not letting them stay here would be best, after all...

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.550
H-Hello, we've come to speak with you.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:35.460
It's Saint.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.880
Oh my, hello.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.460
<i>Maybe I shouldn't let them stay, just like I thought.</i>

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:46.060
You know, Mr. Saint, I'm sorry, but—

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.470
Oh, we understand.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.590
H-Here it is.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:50.720
3 Months Worth of Rent Included
Matsuda Heights Room 201

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.100
It's our rent for the next three months.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.580
My, are you sure about this?

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.580
You don't need to go as far as paying in advance.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.570
No, we felt it was the proper thing to do.

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.740
More importantly...

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:07.150
We weren't able to obtain certification of official registration for a seal...

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.890
We deeply apologize!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.300
Oh...

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.320
That's fine.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.390
You're foreigners, so just a signature would be enough.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.030
Th-That's right!

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.060
We just need to sign.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.630
We're being far too thoughtless.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.640
<i>Huh, maybe they're responsible people, after all.</i>

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.460
Oh, that reminds me. If you'd like, please accept this gift.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.650
My my, I wouldn't feel right accepting...

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.650
Greetings

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.650
Saint

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:41.750
A goat?

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.060
Huh?! I-Is this not acceptable?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.630
It's a rather standard gift where I come from though.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.070
Sheep?

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:51.030
M-Maybe a sheep would've been...

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.620
We don't allow pets here!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.710
Huh?! O-Oh, that's the problem?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.120
W-We're very sorry!

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.810
H-H-Hello? Peter? She said the goat was no good.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.870
I should kick them out, after all.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.140
We apologize for our discourtesy earlier.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.770
Listen, Mr. Saint, I'm sorry, but—

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:14.890
U-Um...

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:16.390
High-Quality
Gold Leaf Green Tea

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:17.440
This is for you.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.650
It isn't anything special, but if you'd like...

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:29.140
This gold leaf green tea got the better of me.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:37.350
Well, I guess just keeping an eye on them is enough for now.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:42.670
Wha—

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.250
Wha—

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.620
What's going on?!

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.050
N-No. N-No, th-this isn't Nirvana or anything.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.130
Jesus Christ!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.300
What in the world was that about?

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.650
Don't tell me...

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.830
He's feeding the birds!

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:20.670
I couldn't care less if they're ninjas, street performers, or ping-pong players.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.180
While they're staying here as tenants of Matsuda Heights,

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:28.960
I'll have them obey the laws here or else!

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.590
Matsuda
Heights

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:31.880
Truth

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.140
<i>Here he comes. It's so late too.</i>

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.750
Just a moment, Mr. Saint.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:49.530
Matsuda
Heights

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.810
G-Good evening.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.280
You're back quite late today.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:46.440
Did work hold you up?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:49.530
N-No, I was out sightseeing.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.030
<i>I wonder when he actually works.</i>

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.770
By the way, Mr. Saint, you haven't been feeding the—

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:06.410
U-Um, th-this, um, is a souvenir. It's for you.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:05.000
Asakusa

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.500
My, how kind of you.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.620
Hold on. Wait right here.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.340
Matsuda
Heights

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.930
Wh-What could it be?

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.680
I wonder if I did something wrong.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.140
Here, take this.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.270
It'd bother me if I was just on the receiving end all the time.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:32.150
It's just some leaftover hydrangea tea.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:35.410
Leaftover...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.750
Hydrangea tea...

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.960
Asakusa

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.710
Matsuda
Heights

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.160
The teacup...

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:52.840
That was...

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.970
Y-Yes?

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.720
Could that have been...

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.930
Y-Y-Yes?

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.430
A magic trick?

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.770
Th-Th-That's right! I-It's just a slight of the hand.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:13.960
U-Um, if you'd like, please help yourself.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.820
M-M-My, all right then.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.320
kusa

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.200
Wait, I forgot to ask about the birds!

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.210
Oh no, my false tooth...

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.550
I need to go see a dentist.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:35.150
But before I do...

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.220
I'll get an answer out of those two!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.100
Grandpa.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.400
<i>He should be back around now.</i>

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.020
He's here.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.330
We'll need to cut down on expenses this month.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.140
Just a moment, Mr. Saint!

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.710
Oh, Ms. Matsuda—

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.740
Matsuda
Heights

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.190
Th-This is...

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.760
It bore food.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:08.820
Huh?

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.960
The peach tree has borne fruit for the first time!

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:12.500
Grandpa...

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:15.130
Grandpa stood up!

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.410
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.410
Grandma!

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.130
Don't be so concerned.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.970
It's not as if I have nothing to eat.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.980
W-Well, it <i>has</i> been rather warm lately.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.840
Th-That's true.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.900
Not again!

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.900
I'm going to ask them this time for sure!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.820
Wh-What's this?

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:47.910
Don't tell me...

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:51.030
They're feeding the cats too?

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.290
Mr. Saint! It's Matsuda, the landlady.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:08.890
Whoa, that's a <i>lot</i> of cats.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:14.650
I had everyone living on the first floor stand with a plate, but they checked out clean.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.420
Here, take it!

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.030
Huh? B-But...

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:21.280
We really didn't feed them or anything.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.680
Huh?! W-Wait, why are you responding to that?

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.070
<i>Looks like I finally caught them.</i>

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.330
I'll have to ask you two to leave here.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.500
N-No way!

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:37.670
Jeez...

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.390
And to think we even have trouble feeding ourselves—

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.080
We would never barbecue a cat!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.900
Look. You even trained them to act.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.480
N-No we didn't—

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.120
Enough with the excuses!

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:11.620
Find anything?

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:13.880
Not in this darkness.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:16.580
Sorry for the trouble, Mr. Saint.

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:18.380
It's no trouble at all.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.850
I'm sure we'll find it soon.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.710
Oh, wh-what about o-over there?

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.500
Huh? Where? I can't really see.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.530
Let's give it a rest.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.940
We won't be able to find it.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:34.670
You two should head back to your room before you catch a cold.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:38.240
But it's important, right?

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:40.950
Exactly. We really don't mind.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.320
Mr. Saint...

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.180
But—

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:51.330
Besides, Ms. Matsuda's happiness is indirectly our happiness as well.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.800
Mr. Saint...

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.090
Buddha, you're...

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:05.110
If you say something that virtuous, your halo will pop up, so stop!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:09.380
What's this light?!

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:10.580
See, I told you!

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.520
Hurry. Hurry up and hide it!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.770
S-S-Sorry!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.920
Oh, a false tooth.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.270
I found it, Ms. Matsuda!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:21.190
My eyes! It's blinding! I can't see anything!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:31.090
<i>And so, the tenth commandment of Matsuda Heights was established.</i>

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:29.160
Matsuda Heights' Commandments
You must pay your rent
You must take your trash out on time
after sorting it
You mustn't forget your daily greetings
You mustn't disturb others with loudness
You must respect your parents
You mustn't disturb your neighbors
You mustn't incite an assembly
You mustn't keep a pet
You mustn't feed stray animals
Excessive Illumination Prohibited

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.390
Now then,

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:39.910
Mr. Saint, I made some simmered vegetables.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.410
<i>The Enlightened One: Buddha.</i>

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.950
<i>The Son of God: Jesus.</i>

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:16.340
<i>A discussion between the two, sharing their wisdom with each other, was reaching its climax.</i>

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.540
The exquisite taste of the cuisine...

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.960
and the internet community are things I refuse to yield on!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.670
I also value their cuisine highly.

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:28.050
Personally, I believe the ideal staple food is rice.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:34.310
However, paella doesn't count as a rice dish! At least to me!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.730
Darn, so it's no good, huh?

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.980
How to Walk in the Lower World

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.150
Spain, that is.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:43.580
Saint☆Young Men.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.740
What a dilemma.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:52.090
We're going on vacation in two months, and we <i>still</i> don't know where we're going.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.080
Oh, how about your home town?

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.190
Isn't it in a rice-producing region?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.410
No, I'd rather not go to India.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.180
Since it wouldn't feel like a vacation?

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.870
No, it's not that.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:07.760
The water's too dirty.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:11.510
That's not something you, who bathed in the Ganges River, should be saying.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:14.920
I've always had a weak stomach,

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:20.710
and after 2400 years of my Nirvana-influenced lifestyle, it's gotten even worse.

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.520
Oh.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:26.860
Well, to be honest, I'm scared of going to India too.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.590
Huh? You too?

00:15:30.770 --> 00:15:36.800
I mean, you know, they say if you go to India, your view of life changes, right?

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:37.960
Yeah, no.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:41.430
You should be less impressionable as is befitting of your position.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:48.200
But honestly, the <i>real</i> problem is going to areas where other religions are widespread.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.380
Yeah, that's definitely a difficult issue.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:56.080
Differences in culture and education make it hard to pick suitable gifts after all.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.570
Yeah, it's really tough to deal with.

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:02.150
A goat's the only thing that comes to mind though.

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:06.570
Besides that, I guess we need to think about the number of people.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.190
Depending on the place, it could be problematic.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.790
Yeah, that's true.

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:17.010
With all that in mind, I'm actually thinking Japan would be the optimal location.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:20.200
Huh?! I-Isn't that place a myriad of gods?!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.980
It wouldn't be a problem of counting how many boxes of macadamia nuts to bring with 8,000,000 gods!

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.560
That's all the more reason.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.200
If we were to bring gifts to <i>all</i> those gods,

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.240
it would actually be considered shameful, right?!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.710
I believe we'll be accepted into the country with just a passport and good intentions.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:44.650
<i>At that moment, it is said that Jesus foresaw that his purse strings would be held in the human world.</i>

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.000
<i>And three months later...</i>

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.360
Good grief, it's really pouring down.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.620
We can't go out to see the cherry blossoms like this.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.420
I wonder if rice-producing regions all get lots of rain.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.160
And you know, speaking of rice...

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.810
Yeah. To think that on a single grain of rice...

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:10.840
Money, money, money.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.840
<i>Really, Japanese rice is the best.</i>

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:14.680
<i>Oh, but I'm sorry. We didn't bring any gifts with us.</i>

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.470
<i>Yes, yes. Honestly.</i>

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.470
<i>There are seven gods on a single grain of rice.</i>

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.930
Yes, exactly.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:24.090
I honestly regretted not bringing any gifts with us.

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:28.010
But I think it was the right choice coming to Japan.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:28.940
Agreed.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.130
The rice is delicious, and it has four seasons too.

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:36.640
But still, it really does rain a lot.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.200
Samson
and
Delilah

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.200
Siddhartha

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.720
It's getting troublesome hanging up the laundry indoors.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:44.960
I don't think you should be washing the winter clothes too just because you're bored, Buddha.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:49.040
There's nothing else left seeing as how the ventilation fan and sink are already sparkly clean.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.760
Uh, yeah. That's not what I'm getting at.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.810
When you're bored, you always busy yourself with chores.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:18:01.010
Babel

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.410
You should find a hobby to enjoy at home.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:59.450
Even I have a hobby or two.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.010
Oh? Like what?

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.920
Zen meditation and sutra chanting.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:06.530
No, I mean something that won't make your halo pop out.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:09.880
In that case...

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.090
<i>Maybe silk screening?</i>

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:18.280
Jeez, you won't last long if you treat your work like a hobby.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:22.160
You have no idea that a third of all the T-shirts we have were printed by me, Jesus.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.060
That reminds me.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:30.080
It's been bugging me, but what do you always do on your laptop?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:36.090
Joshua

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:36.090
White
Elephant

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:36.090
Samson
and
Delilah

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.960
Siddhartha

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:34.190
Whenever you have free time, you open your laptop—

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:40.970
Sujata

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:37.820
Jesus?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:44.000
I wouldn't suspect you of it, but you're not doing anything a god would be ashamed of, right?

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.040
N-Not at all. Of course not!

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.600
Don't worry. I've done nothing to deserve a Zen stick beating.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.540
<i>I did look up Momoiro Clover Z once though.</i>

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:57.240
I-It's not that. Uh, Buddha, do you know what a "blog" is?

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:00.700
I do.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.540
It's something like a diary, right?

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:03.530
Are you writing one?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.020
Y-Yeah, I am.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.690
Truth is, I was even while we were in Heaven.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.210
Jessa's
Dramandala!!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.660
Oh? That's amazing.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:13.390
I'm guessing it's about your impressions of dramas?

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:14.680
Yeah, exactly.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.320
But it's also much more than that.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:24.340
I watch the dramas on every channel at every time slot, and write posts on that exact day.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:28.330
It's a popular blog that boasts 10,000 hits every day!

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:32.790
<i>If gods have that much free time, it must mean the world is at peace.</i>

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.770
Someday, it'll become the number one blog.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:36.450
Oh, you're not using your real name, I see.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.820
Naturally.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.500
So at first, nobody was reading it,

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:44.150
but when the comments started building up bit by bit...

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.280
<i>I've decided to follow you!</i>

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.090
<i>Me too!</i>

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.780
It reminded me of back when I was propagating.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:52.000
Oh? That sounds sort of nice.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.090
Oh, looks like the commenters are pretty lively.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:59.050
Yeah, and I make sure to answer any questions.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:01.720
God has descended!!

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.840
You <i>do</i> hide your real name, right?

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:08.340
Sure do...

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:17.890
I feel hungry all of a sudden after updating my blog.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:21.280
Young Priest Miri

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:21.280
Sesame Seeds

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.090
All we have is seasoning, laver, sesame seeds, and underpants.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.960
Jesus, you still chill your underpants?

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.860
Once you give it a try, you just can't go back to wearing lukewarm underpants, after all.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.420
We have ready-made pouches of milk gruel if you want.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.430
Huh? <i>Still</i>?

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.010
Buddha, you really like that, huh?

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:53.730
Joshua

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:46.610
No, it's just that there's someone who sends it to me every year for the Bon Festival.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.390
Oh, Ms. Sujata?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:48.970
Yeah.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:53.300
She's the first person that made milk gruel for me, but...

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:58.210
Because of my asceticism at the time, I was the hungriest I could possibly get.

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:02.020
And they do say hunger is the best spice.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.020
<i>Delicious!</i>

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:07.260
She sends it to me every year, so now it's too late to ask her to stop!

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:12.160
But I really can't stand that peculiar stench it has!

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:16.050
She's quite faithful to have kept it up for 2500 years.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:18.400
The situation can only get worse from here on out.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.240
Oh, that's not good. I'm really starving now.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.360
Guess I should go out for food.

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:35.230
But I'd rather not go out in the rain.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:40.390
Oh, that's right! Hey, Buddha, what about deliver—

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:41.280
Jesus.

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:44.010
There's no rain that never ceases.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:48.760
Even if you're hungry, if you go to sleep, tomorrow will surely come.

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:54.940
Don't shoot a Buddha smile at me while
double-clicking at a time like this, Buddha.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:00.460
Well, sure, you might be okay with it since you're a fasting specialist.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.790
Besides, it's only four o'clock.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.150
Even if I tried to sleep, I wouldn't be able to.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:07.200
Jeez, fine.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:11.180
And I was right in the middle of looking at a site about healthy eating habits.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:14.510
Wait here. I'll go get something, okay?

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:17.020
H-Huh? H-Hey, what? Buddha?

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:22.700
I-Is he going shopping on his own?

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:26.010
No, I couldn't let you do that. I'm not that—

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:30.310
Wait, wh-what?

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:31.120
Where did you go?

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.410
Here, it's dinner.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.150
Buddha. This...

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:41.040
Huh?

00:22:41.550 --> 00:22:44.380
You can make rocks into bread and water into wine, right?

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:48.720
That doesn't mean you should serve this to me like some sort of demon wife!

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:52.130
Wouldn't it be fine if you just make it turn into yakisoba bread or some other filling bread?

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:55.750
Anything aside from rye bread is outside my field of expertise!

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:00.740
It's Matsuda, the landlady!

00:23:00.740 --> 00:23:02.530
The la—

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:04.330
Wait, the landlady?

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:06.370
We paid the rent already, right?

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:07.830
We did!

00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:09.290
Then what could it be?

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:10.450
Think we did something wrong?

00:23:11.110 --> 00:23:15.080
Our background is completely obscure, so we had a tough time entering the country too!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:18.620
I-It's all right. We've been living peacefully.

00:23:21.930 --> 00:23:24.320
I-It's fine. We don't have to feel guilty.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.260
First, hide that thing somehow.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.520
The Buddha statue we won at the lottery.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:42.350
Otherwise, she'll think we're part of some weird religious group or serious narcissists!

00:23:44.030 --> 00:23:46.940
<i>If she did say we were part of a religious group, it'd be pretty hard to deny.</i>

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:49.700
Great.

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:59.000
Saint

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:57.600
Hello, Mr. Saint?

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:58.770
Yes!

00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:01.340
Oh my.

00:24:01.340 --> 00:24:02.840
My, you were actually here?

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:05.730
It's a weekday too.

00:24:05.730 --> 00:24:07.880
What about work?

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.670
<i>Now she suspects us of being NEETs.</i>

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.580
<i>Suspected of being a narcissist or suspected of being a NEET.</i>

00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:17.840
<i>Just which of the two would have been better?</i>

00:24:19.630 --> 00:24:24.620
<i>It's said that later that day, the two consulted Mary in Heaven about it.</i>
